{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/797178-oneiromancy","id":797178,"title":"Oneiromancy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-30T21:19:41-08:00","id":797178,"title":"Oneiromancy","content":"Suppose a changeling is unlucky enough to get targeted by a rampaging horror one night and gets his dream self pulled into a lair. Also, suppose this changeling is skilled in Oneiromancy/dream manipulation. Naturally the changeling is going to decide he doesn't want to have a nightmare tonight and tries to make it a more pleasing dream. What happens at this point? My storyteller and I have been pondering this for a while, just some theory crafting while we wait for mage, and we can't really come up with a clear answer. We're pretty sure the horror should be able to resist any attempts at modifying its lair but other than that we've got nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T00:08:57-08:00","id":797218,"title":"","content":"Does this default to clash of wills?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T01:05:06-08:00","id":797229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/797178-oneiromancy?p=797218#post797218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this default to clash of wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>It defaults to &quot;the Lair is not a dream.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T02:55:34-08:00","id":797249,"title":"","content":"I think it would end up with the Changeling trying to change what he thinks is a dream, failing and making the Horror angry. Not good for Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T03:55:08-08:00","id":797266,"title":"","content":"The Horror leaves her Lair to visit other's dreams, not pull others into her Lair. Furthermore, the way that Changelings deal with dreams is idfferent than visiting through the Astral. Mundane dreams aren't part of the Temnos / Primordial Dream, despite the name. Two completely different regions. Furthermore, proper dreams are kind of a border area that touch on a lot of different regions, and are not quite inside individual Onerios either.<br /> <br /> In short, what you're doing simply doesn't have rules or expectations with it. The Astral has never been shaped like a dream, and I don't expect it to change with 2e rules. As things stand, the Fae cannot use their oneriomancy inside the Astral proper. They can only do it in the areas where dreams touch on the Hedge / Faerie. If a changeling is pulled entirely into the Temnos, then they cannot dreamshape.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even in Mage, there was a clear demarkation between dreams and the Astral. You can use a simple Mind 3 spell ( I think it was 3) to enter a dream. You need other ways to enter the Astral proper, such as a Hallow or Artifact. Its a common misunderstanding to assume they're linked. They're not. Dreams are kind of a borderland that touch on so many different regions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-31-2015, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T11:36:51-08:00","id":797441,"title":"","content":"According to &quot;Astral Realms&quot; changeling dream shaping powers work just fine in the Onieros, pg 138 if you'd like to check, so we assumed they'd work in the Primordial Dream. If that's not the case then is the changeling just screwed in this scenario?<br /> <br /> @MCN<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Success: </b>The Horror inflicts dreams of its presence and Hunger on the targeted individual. He loses a point of Willpower, while the Beast gains 1 Satiety. The target awakens feeling restless and disturbed, but (at least after <i>one </i>such dream), with no lasting damage.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The Horror, not satisfied with a simple nightmares, seizes the targeted individual and drags him into the Lair via a Primordial Pathway. The Horror then hunts down the individual and attempts to \u201ckill\u201d him. If he loses all Astral Health within the Lair, the Beast gains the victim\u2019s Willpower dots in Satiety. When the victim awakens, he has the Soul Shocked Condition (p. XX). Any Heroes in the region can attempt to track the Beast, as described in Chapter Five.</span> </div> </div> </div>I had forgotten that there were two possible results of success for the horrors hunt. This also makes me wonder how this scenario plays out if the horror is 'just' causing a nightmare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T17:14:00-08:00","id":797559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/797178-oneiromancy?p=797441#post797441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to &quot;Astral Realms&quot; changeling dream shaping powers work just fine in the Onieros, pg 138 if you'd like to check, so we assumed they'd work in the Primordial Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a segment saying that changelings affect people through messing around in their unconscious in a different fashion from how astral travel works in Mage's framework. There's a similar note in Book of the Dead's section on the Grave Dream.<br /> <br /> The Oneiros is experienced in a comparable manner to dreams, being a series of vistas that debatably don't exist without someone to observe them, which cannot be said for the Lair, which exists in its entirety regardless of the attention of the Beast or any visitors they may have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T07:17:34-08:00","id":797797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/797178-oneiromancy?p=797441#post797441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to &quot;Astral Realms&quot; changeling dream shaping powers work just fine in the Onieros, pg 138 if you'd like to check, so we assumed they'd work in the Primordial Dream. If that's not the case then is the changeling just screwed in this scenario?</div> </div> </div> </div> That section basically state that changeigns interact with dreams differenlty than mages do. Dreams do touch on the Onerios, but they're not part of the Onerios. Dreams also are part of the Hedge/Faerie in a way that they're not linked to the Astral. And vampires interact with dreams in a different way than either of the two previous.<br /> <br /> In either case, the section flat out says that changelings are barred from the Temnos, which is where the Primordial Dream IS. The dark dreams of humanity. Changelings have no contract or resonance there. So, yes, they're screwed if they get dragged in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I had forgotten that there were two possible results of success for the horrors hunt. This also makes me wonder how this scenario plays out if the horror is 'just' causing a nightmare. </div> </div> </div> Huh, I forgot about the exceptional success part. Still, that part implies that a Beast can just show up in the dream and psychically &quot;drag&quot; a changeling out of their own dreams without a fight. That would be a fight that I can't imagine such a hungry dragon would be interested in engaging in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T12:13:29-08:00","id":797914,"title":"","content":"Doesn't even have to be the Changeling's dream, if I'm understanding this bit from pg 98 right. <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">Beasts aren\u2019t the only beings in the World of Darkness who can walk between worlds. Any supernatural being accessing the dreams or soul of someone inside the Lair can find themselves in the Primordial Dream, from changelings caught up when a Beast preys on a dream... </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So if the Changeling uses a pledge to enter a human's dream and that human has been dragged into the Lair, the Changeling ends up there too.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I've been wondering if forging a Dreaming pledge with a Beast would allow a Changeling to access the Lair (I'm assuming Be My Guest would be part of the pledge).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T13:26:11-08:00","id":797944,"title":"","content":"Changelings don't see the Oneiros. They see the [Redacted] connected in the Skein.<br /> <br /> As Brookshaw has pointed out, the Skein in general is this high floating level that blends between simple dreams and the first layer of the Astral. Changelings regularly walk around the Skein, this amalgamation of the two, and regularly futz around with it, pulling off deep tricks that mages and other creature would simply have to go deeper for, and also have greater mobility than most in that sphere-but a changeling's power extends to the powerful inner worlds of sentiment in each person, not in the that weird mass where people lose individuality called the Temenos. The Dark Dream beyond that, where humanity as a species on the whole interacts with the world, is something kind of beyond them.<br /> <br /> As it stands now, as far as canon goes, changelings just lack the infrastructure to effectively <i>move</i> what Beast's deal with. if their Horror is appropriating a dream to get their feeding done, a changeling wandering that dream is going to find it too heavy to shift. Heaven help them if they end up in the Lair.<br /> <br /> Now, as house rules go, I'd still let them try, and they even have a sort of edge, but we'll come back to that. Oneiromancy can be done, but with penalties, equal to Satiety if it's a Beast in another person's dream, Lair if they're in the Lair. This is just a quick and fast thing, and I wouldn't keep to that. The advantage that changelings have, though, is that they can actively leverage things, they can act and change. A Beast is too bound to their Horror and Lair to do so, so they never get to contest.<br /> <br /> One other thing? A changeling, while dreamwalking, is as powerful as they always are. The Beast, in the meantime, has moments of power and moments of weakness. They flux in ways changelings don't. That can be an advantage or a disadvantage for the changeling, depending where they are at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T13:37:27-08:00","id":797946,"title":"","content":"Like, as a nutshell, the Temenos and Primordial Dream are just too gnarled and rooted for changelings to lift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T13:42:05-08:00","id":797951,"title":"","content":"If I was playing a Changeling and found myself in a Beast's Lair, I wouldn't ask my ST what could I do with dream crafting. I'd ask what could I do with talecrafting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T13:47:48-08:00","id":797956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/797178-oneiromancy?p=797951#post797951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was playing a Changeling and found myself in a Beast's Lair, I wouldn't ask my ST what could I do with dream crafting. I'd ask what could I do with talecrafting?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would definitely get you places, I feel. It's probably the better tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T13:53:57-08:00","id":797957,"title":"","content":"Hypothetically speaking, how could a changeling go further than just &quot;looking at the windows and front yard&quot; (searching through dreams) and actually &quot;go into the house&quot; (enter the Oneiros)? I do agree with making the Temenos beyond the reach of changelings, barring very strange circumstances.<br /> <br /> If I'm not mistaken, Astral Realms said that the Gentry don't have dreams. I also saw DaveB mentioning on RPGnet that the True Fae sometimes appear inside the Dreamtime/Anima Mundi, kinda like the Uratha. Does this mean the True Fae have no Oneiroi to use against them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T14:02:02-08:00","id":797960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/797178-oneiromancy?p=797956#post797956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would definitely get you places, I feel. It's probably the better tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awww yeah <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm still hoping Ride to Damascus will actually be plasuible when the cannon metaphysics &amp; mechanics are released.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T14:03:17-08:00","id":797962,"title":"","content":"Again, changelings don't see a difference. Few changelings think they actually tamper with souls, but Oneiromancy does just that. Dreams and Oneiros might as well be one for changelings, it's just a matter of how hard they 'lift'.<br /> <br /> And considering the Strangers are living stories? Yeah, no, they have no Oneiroi. I'm not even sure how they function within the Astral Realms, to be honest. Chnagelings have been explored in mage terms plenty, but the Strangers? Not as much. It's hard for me to lump them together. Still, I would say you couldn't find a 'place' for them in the astral, because their existence works similarly to Beasts, their Domains in Arcadia looking a lot like Beast's Lairs in the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> But Arcadia's not an Astral Realm, so I would say those instance are just them passing through where their story lets them walk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T14:23:54-08:00","id":797977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/797178-oneiromancy?p=797962#post797962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, changelings don't see a difference. Few changelings think they actually tamper with souls, but Oneiromancy does just that. Dreams and Oneiros might as well be one for changelings, it's just a matter of how hard they 'lift'.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not sure if I understand what you mean by &quot;lift&quot;. Could you please rephrase? I'm just asking because I'm worried I might have made one of my fae characters approach dreams in a way more similar to mages exploring Oneiroi.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T14:35:30-08:00","id":797981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/797178-oneiromancy?p=797977#post797977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not sure if I understand what you mean by &quot;lift&quot;. Could you please rephrase? I'm just asking because I'm worried I might have made one of my fae characters approach dreams in a way more similar to mages exploring Oneiroi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings doing oneiromancy could, on one hand, be messing with the incidental set dressings, or there again they could be poking around in the actual contents of a person's soul. Whether surface appearances have a meaningful connection to deeper processes is variable when it comes to the fae and largely comes down to matters of intent and/or fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T14:59:30-08:00","id":797994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/797178-oneiromancy?p=797981#post797981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings doing oneiromancy could, on one hand, be messing with the incidental set dressings, or there again they could be poking around in the actual contents of a person's soul. Whether surface appearances have a meaningful connection to deeper processes is variable when it comes to the fae and largely comes down to matters of intent and/or fate.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, the Oneiros my PC explored and protected belonged to a skilled lucid dreamer, and there were lots of appropriately oneiric symbolism going on, so I guess it's no big deal if it ended up looking a bit mage-y. That might even be a plot hook, now that I think about. Some hobgoblins might have been humans or changelings that had too much ripped away from them by the Thorns, right? And if dreams are an important part of the soul, the habit of certain hobgoblins and incubi of invading dreams might be an attempt to restore something they lost. I think Autumn Nightmares or Dancers In The Dusk acknowledged this as possible, but I'm not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}